<title>SWITZERLAND: Audi sees 1997 A6 sales at 60,000 units.</title>
<headline>Audi sees 1997 A6 sales at 60,000 units.</headline>
<dateline>GENEVA 1997-03-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>German carmaker Audi AG, a unit of Volkswagen AG, said on Tuesday it planned to sell more than 60,000 of its new A6 saloons in 1997 and for sales to grow initially to 130,000 units in 1998.</p>
<p>&quot;A sales volume of over 60,000 A6 units is planned for the current year,&quot; Audi deputy management board chairman Franz-Josef Paefgen said in a speech at the Geneva car show to unveil the new Audi saloon.</p>
<p>&quot;For 1998, we will aim at a sales target of 130,000 cars initially.&quot;</p>
<p>--John Gilardi, Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
